{"title":"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 26","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Julie runs a website where she sells university themed clothing. On Monday, she sells thirteen Stanford sweatshirts and nine Harvard sweatshirts for a total of &#36;370. On Tuesday, she sells nine Stanford sweatshirts and two Harvard sweatshirts for a total of &#36;180. On Wednesday, she sells twelve Stanford sweatshirts and six Harvard sweatshirts. If Julie didn't change the prices of any items all week, how much money did she take in (total number of dollars) from the sale of Stanford and Harvard sweatshirts on Wednesday? \n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be cost of Stanford clothing, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be cost of Harvard clothing.  From the given information,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/7/327814afbfdfbfea231d9a2fe03924f5350ea834.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[13s + 9h = 370\\]\" width=\"117\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7a2b40749f60fe7b0c34bba050fb801a8beeb85.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9s + 2h = 180\\]\" width=\"109\" height=\"14\" />\nAdd the two equations to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9ca98a018b7380d71bdbe6d174185b8860b93ebc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[22s + 11h = 550\\]\" width=\"127\" height=\"14\" />\nMultiply both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/3/063cb9fa3f9c1a13cdde7a7aad39b8464a93424e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/d/eddcc86601b066fc35d82199658cc8c2aea8855f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[12s + 6h = 300\\]\" width=\"117\" height=\"14\" />\nThus, Julie earns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/e/7fed1da2e7d36709fa32647fcc0b0e33128926b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\$300}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"48\" height=\"26\" /> on Wednesday.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest\" title=\"2007 iTest\">2007 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 iTest Answer Key\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Pro